#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""blockcheck - is a domain (or *.wildcard) actually blocked?

Stdlib only, no dig/host required: ships its own DNS client. Probes four
independent layers and tells you *where* the block happens, not just that
something failed:

  dns     local resolver vs public resolvers vs DoH vs authoritative NS
          (NXDOMAIN, SERVFAIL, REFUSED, NODATA, sinkhole 0.0.0.0/loopback,
           private-IP rewrite, silent drop, transparent interception)
  cname   full CNAME chain, cross-domain hops, known tracker/vendor targets,
          first-party CNAME cloaking, and CNAME targets that are themselves
          blocked (a classic "site hangs for 30s" cause)
  tcp/tls TCP connect + TLS handshake per address with SNI: distinguishes an
          IP/port block from SNI-based filtering from a MITM/block portal
  http    block-page fingerprinting when TLS fails or DNS is sinkholed

Examples
  blockcheck example.com
  blockcheck '*.doubleclick.net'
  blockcheck example.com -v --auth --asn
  blockcheck -f domains.txt --json > report.json
  blockcheck ads.site.com --resolver 192.168.31.1:53 --timeout 3
  blockcheck '*.example.com' --samples 5 --brief

Exit codes: 0 allowed, 2 blocked, 3 partial/unknown, 1 error.
"""

